                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>A fourth meeting in 1954 of the ANZUS Council
                    Deputies was held in Washington on August 10. The participants of the three
                    powers were led by Under Secretary Smith and Ambassadors Spender and Munro. Sir
                    Robert Scott and Joy attended the meeting as “informal observers” for the United
                    Kingdom. The discussion centered on procedural matters relating to the proposed
                    Southeast Asia Collective Defense Treaty. United States minutes of <pb
                        facs="0734" n="716" xml:id="pg716"/> the meeting, drafted by Foster, are in
                    Conference files, lot 60 D 627, CF 355.</p>
            </div>
